    "### 10. Monte Carlo Integration for High Dimensions"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Volume of 10-dimensional hypersphere: points inside [-1, 1]^10 with L2 norm <= 1\n",
    "# Analytical volume of 10D hypersphere is pi^5 / 5! = (pi^5) / 120 = 2.550164\n",
    "for N in [10**4, 10**5, 10**6]:\n",
    "    pts = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, (N, 10))\n",
    "    inside = np.sum(pts**2, axis=1) <= 1.0\n",
    "    fraction = np.sum(inside) / N\n",
    "    # Volume of bounding box is 2^10 = 1024\n",
    "    volume_est = fraction * 1024\n",
    "    print(f\"N = {N}: Estimated Volume = {volume_est:.4f} (True: 2.5502)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 11. Importance Sampling"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import scipy.stats as stats\n",
    "\n",
    "N = 100000\n",
    "# Sample from proposal q\n",
    "q_samples = np.random.normal(0, np.sqrt(2), N)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute weight w(x) = p(x) / q(x)\n",
    "p_density = stats.norm.pdf(q_samples, loc=2, scale=1)\n",
    "q_density = stats.norm.pdf(q_samples, loc=0, scale=np.sqrt(2))\n",
    "weights = p_density / q_density\n",
    "\n",
    "# estimate E[x^2] for x~p\n",
    "# True value is Var(x) + E[x]^2 = 1 + 2^2 = 5\n",
    "est = np.mean(q_samples**2 * weights)\n",
    "print(f\"Importance sampling estimate: {est:.4f} (True: 5.0)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 12. Cholesky Factorization for Jitter\n",
    "Due to roundoff error, a theoretical covariance matrix $K$ might have tiny negative eigenvalues, causing Cholesky factorization to fail. \n",
    "Adding a small positive value $\\epsilon$ to the diagonal (known as **jitter**, typically $\\epsilon = 10^{-6} \\times I$) shifts all eigenvalues up by $\\epsilon$, restoring positive definiteness:\n",
    "$$\\lambda_i(K + \\epsilon I) = \\lambda_i(K) + \\epsilon > 0$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "K = np.array([[1.0, 1.0], [1.0, 1.0]])  # rank 1, positive semi-definite\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    np.linalg.cholesky(K)\n",
    "except np.linalg.LinAlgError as e:\n",
    "    print(\"Cholesky failed as expected!\", e)\n",
    "    \n",
    "K_jitter = K + 1e-8 * np.eye(2)\n",
    "L = np.linalg.cholesky(K_jitter)\n",
    "print(\"Cholesky succeeded with jitter:\\n\", L)"
   ]
  },
  {
